- I guess I’m about to get my ass whooped.

00:01:08.651 --> 00:01:10.779
- You start your career in New York with the Jets.

00:01:10.779 --> 00:01:12.906
A whole lotta headlines that came out when you was in New York, 

00:01:12.906 --> 00:01:14.115
during the Rex Ryan era.

00:01:14.115 --> 00:01:14.616
- Oh, for sure.

00:01:14.616 --> 00:01:15.784
- Rex Ryan, Bart Scott, 

00:01:15.784 --> 00:01:18.495
there was always something interesting that was gonna come out of that locker room.

00:01:18.495 --> 00:01:20.622
- No doubt. We had some characters on the team.

00:01:20.622 --> 00:01:21.581
- So talk to me. 

00:01:21.581 --> 00:01:22.707
Jets-Patriots. 

00:01:22.707 --> 00:01:25.210
Always a very competitive, fierce game. 

00:01:25.210 --> 00:01:26.586
Rex Ryan, Bill Belichick. 

00:01:26.586 --> 00:01:28.671
This one happens to be on “Monday Night Football.”

00:01:28.671 --> 00:01:30.256
What's going in leading up to the game?

00:01:30.256 --> 00:01:31.925
&nbsp;- We felt we were prepared.

00:01:31.925 --> 00:01:34.094
We felt we had a great game plan,

00:01:34.094 --> 00:01:36.513
but that was probably one of the worst games I’ve ever played. 

00:01:36.513 --> 00:01:38.723
We got embarrassed. We lost 45-3.

00:01:38.723 --> 00:01:40.975
Tom shredded us. We couldn’t really do much. 

00:01:40.975 --> 00:01:42.727
We had no momentum that game.

00:01:42.727 --> 00:01:44.896
- I cut that game off at halftime, bro, to be honest with you.

00:01:44.896 --> 00:01:46.064
I stopped watching at halftime.

00:01:46.731 --> 00:01:48.233
- It's a backstory to this.

00:01:48.233 --> 00:01:51.194
We had a team meeting the next day, and 

00:01:51.194 --> 00:01:52.737
the coaching staff is pissed off.

00:01:52.737 --> 00:01:55.198
Rex is going through plays, our mistakes.

00:01:55.198 --> 00:01:56.991
We were all disgusted about the film. 

00:01:56.991 --> 00:01:59.536
Its 45-3, you couldn’t—

00:01:59.536 --> 00:02:00.537
- [Laughing] What you gonna watch?

00:02:00.537 --> 00:02:00.954
- Yeah.

00:02:00.954 --> 00:02:04.290
He got so pissed off, he was like, “Everybody, meet me outside right now!” 

00:02:04.290 --> 00:02:07.085
We’re like, “Meet you on the practice field? Like, OK.” 

00:02:07.085 --> 00:02:09.170
We meet him out on the practice field. 

00:02:09.170 --> 00:02:11.506
He’s kinda a little bit ahead of us.

00:02:11.506 --> 00:02:13.508
We see him walking to this ditch.

00:02:13.508 --> 00:02:16.052
We’re like, “What's up? What's going on?”

00:02:16.052 --> 00:02:18.096
- How many guys are outside now at this point?

00:02:18.096 --> 00:02:22.308
- It’s coaching staff, team, trainers, might have been. I don’t know, this is—&nbsp;

00:02:22.308 --> 00:02:23.393
- Probably the ones digging the ditch.

00:02:23.393 --> 00:02:24.644
- A huge group of people.

00:02:24.644 --> 00:02:27.647
He stops in front of the ditch, saying his speech. 

00:02:27.647 --> 00:02:31.317
“We got embarrassed. I know you guys are better than this, 

00:02:31.317 --> 00:02:32.235
blah, blah, blah, blah. 

00:02:32.235 --> 00:02:34.320
We can do better as a coaching staff.” 

00:02:34.320 --> 00:02:36.531
Another assistant coach handed him the ball.

00:02:36.531 --> 00:02:37.699
This was the game ball. 

00:02:37.699 --> 00:02:40.243
He was like, “I’m gonna tell you guys right now, 

00:02:40.243 --> 00:02:41.953
this will never happen again!” 

00:02:41.953 --> 00:02:45.623
He’s, like, chanting with the ball and, you know, waving it back and forth.

00:02:45.623 --> 00:02:49.919
He’s like, “We’re gonna bury this ball right here, as a coaching staff, as a team.” 

00:02:49.919 --> 00:02:51.129
Buries the ball,

00:02:51.129 --> 00:02:54.549
and then the guy’s over there putting the dirt on it.

00:02:54.549 --> 00:02:55.383
- [Laughing] Who’s doing that?

00:02:55.383 --> 00:02:59.387
- One of the landscapers obviously that works for the Jets.

00:02:59.387 --> 00:03:01.514
We’re just sitting there like,&nbsp;looking like, 

00:03:01.514 --> 00:03:03.224
“He really just bury the ball? 

00:03:03.224 --> 00:03:06.186
I’ve never seen this before. Like, this is different.”

00:03:06.186 --> 00:03:07.228
- What's going on in your mind?

00:03:07.228 --> 00:03:11.316
- It’s very dramatic. It’s psychological as well. But it worked.

00:03:11.482 --> 00:03:12.150
- Why did it work?

00:03:12.150 --> 00:03:14.819
- We end up playing ‘em in the divisional playoffs.

00:03:14.819 --> 00:03:15.403
- What happens?

00:03:15.737 --> 00:03:18.114
- We won, 28-21.

00:03:18.114 --> 00:03:22.660
And I think that's what fueled us is, you know, Rex’s speech, him burying the ball. 

00:03:22.660 --> 00:03:24.162
It was the magical ball.

00:03:24.162 --> 00:03:25.330
- [Laughing]

00:03:25.330 --> 00:03:26.456
- For us to win. 

00:03:26.956 --> 00:03:28.541
That was the superstition of it.

00:03:28.541 --> 00:03:29.083
- [Laughing]

00:03:29.083 --> 00:03:32.003
- We were celebrating around all of Gillette Stadium, and

00:03:32.003 --> 00:03:33.922
Bart Scott's slogan came out, 

00:03:33.922 --> 00:03:34.923
the “I can’t wait!”

00:03:36.007 --> 00:03:38.176
- Why do you feel like that ball was so magical, 

00:03:38.176 --> 00:03:40.094
where it motivated the team moving forward?

00:03:40.094 --> 00:03:44.724
- I think at that moment, it would’ve made or broke our season.

00:03:44.724 --> 00:03:46.517
We could’ve went into a slump. 

00:03:46.517 --> 00:03:47.518
That was Rex’s touch.

00:03:47.518 --> 00:03:48.519
- [Laughing]

00:03:48.519 --> 00:03:49.395
- And it worked.

00:03:49.395 --> 00:03:50.521
- Where do you think that ball is right now?

00:03:50.521 --> 00:03:54.317
- I probably need to call Jets management and see if the ball is still buried there.

00:03:54.317 --> 00:03:55.860
It might be, it might be.

00:03:55.860 --> 00:03:56.527
- [Laughing]

00:03:56.527 --> 00:03:57.153
- It might be.

00:03:57.153 --> 00:03:58.696
Have you made any balls yet?

00:03:58.696 --> 00:03:59.530
- Oh, yeah, I made one. 

00:03:59.530 --> 00:04:01.658
Come on, you’re gonna have to give me more credit than that now.

00:04:02.075 --> 00:04:03.618
How many years did you spend on the Jets?

00:04:03.743 --> 00:04:05.662
- The New York Jets, I was there for eight years.

00:04:05.662 --> 00:04:06.913
- You hit free agency. 

00:04:06.913 --> 00:04:08.373
Who calling your phone from New England?

00:04:08.373 --> 00:04:10.917
- At the beginning of it, I was kinda like, 

00:04:10.917 --> 00:04:14.045
“Ah, I don’t really feel it,” because of the rivalry.

00:04:14.045 --> 00:04:15.713
- Does that really matter to athletes like that?

00:04:15.713 --> 00:04:16.673
- For me, it did.

00:04:16.673 --> 00:04:18.716
For example, I’m gonna use “Space Jam.”

00:04:18.716 --> 00:04:22.303
If I played for the Monstars, that's the team I’m representing.

00:04:22.303 --> 00:04:24.180
- You switch over to Tune Squad.

00:04:24.180 --> 00:04:26.849
- Yeah. So yeah, you switch over to Tune Squad, then, 

00:04:26.849 --> 00:04:28.768
you know, that’s the squad you playing for. 

00:04:28.768 --> 00:04:31.396
But when business sets in and the numbers come back,

00:04:31.396 --> 00:04:33.648
I decided to team up with the Patriots.

00:04:33.648 --> 00:04:34.941
Corner pocket.

00:04:36.359 --> 00:04:38.027
- What's Bill Belichick like?

00:04:38.027 --> 00:04:40.822
- It’s eggshells. You’re walking on eggshells when you come here.

00:04:40.822 --> 00:04:41.656
- [Laughing]

00:04:41.656 --> 00:04:45.410
- Bill might come out of the blue, ask you some question. 

00:04:45.410 --> 00:04:48.913
Like, it goes back to just they want you to know everything about 

00:04:48.913 --> 00:04:51.207
the preparation or the game day.

00:04:51.207 --> 00:04:54.294
I remember one time he asked me a question during a team meeting, 

00:04:54.294 --> 00:04:56.296
and he was like, “2-4!”

00:04:56.296 --> 00:04:58.423
- [Laughing]

00:04:58.423 --> 00:05:01.843
- "What is Calvin Johnson's average per catch?”

00:05:01.843 --> 00:05:04.178
You’re like, “14.7,” you know.

00:05:04.178 --> 00:05:06.723
“How many yards he have so far this year? 

00:05:06.723 --> 00:05:08.766
How many touchdowns?"

00:05:08.766 --> 00:05:10.101
“I don’t know, 10.” 

00:05:10.101 --> 00:05:13.646
If he could play football, trust me, I mean, he would love to go out there. 

00:05:13.646 --> 00:05:17.233
His mental and his preparation is so competitive. 

00:05:17.233 --> 00:05:20.820
I mean, he put on film from 1940. 

00:05:20.820 --> 00:05:23.781
“I’ve been running this for 40 years!” 

00:05:23.781 --> 00:05:26.743
We’re sitting there looking at black-and-white TV like, 

00:05:27.660 --> 00:05:28.578
“Wait, what?” 

00:05:28.578 --> 00:05:31.748
You gotta give him his respect. That’s why he's a Hall of Famer.

00:05:32.749 --> 00:05:33.750
No shot.

00:05:36.961 --> 00:05:37.712
- C’mon, bro.

00:05:37.712 --> 00:05:38.379
- You caught that.

00:05:38.379 --> 00:05:39.380
- C’mon, bro.

00:05:39.380 --> 00:05:40.381
- I hope you captured that.

00:05:40.381 --> 00:05:41.049
- C’mon, man.

00:05:41.049 --> 00:05:41.716
- You saw that.

